# @ t_odo< "what" stops the program with error[panic] and "not yet
# implemented: what"; it types wherever it stands (Rust's todo!).
== SOURCE
u:a_rea := { r -> r < 0 ? @ t_odo< "negative sizes"; r * r }
u:a_rea 3
u:a_rea -1
== EXPAND
u:a_rea := { r -> r < 0 ? (([]P_ANIC ("not yet implemented: negative sizes"))); r * r }
u:a_rea 3
u:a_rea -1
== ERROR
error[panic]: not yet implemented: negative sizes at 26..51
